{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787992643372,"sessionID":"ses_fb3594f94ffeQ3bCtRbhDqaOUL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_e6107aedb1934ca0b3d2f400","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/web-ui/README.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/web-ui/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # manigot web UI\n2: \n3: The control-plane client for `mg serve` — a Svelte 5 single-page app that\n4: renders the daemon's read-only API today and the mutating surface as it lands.\n5: It is a port of the TUI's information design: same data, same job pipeline,\n6: same attention ordering — built for a browser, so the \"review from a phone,\n7: get a ping when a job needs you, act on it\" story has a surface.\n8: \n9: ## Running\n10: \n11: ```sh\n12: npm install\n13: npm run dev        # vite dev server on :5173\n14: npm run dev:mock   # same, with the in-browser mock daemon (no mg serve needed)\n15: npm run build      # production build to dist/\n16: npm run test       # vitest suite\n17: ```\n18: \n19: The app talks to the daemon through the connection setting (Settings modal /\n20: `?api=` URL param). The daemon is a same-origin JSON API — it sends no CORS\n21: headers, so the browser blocks any direct cross-origin URL (the error will\n22: say \"cross-origin URL blocked\"). In dev, use the vite proxy path instead:\n23: \n24: ```sh\n25: npm run dev\n26: # open http://localhost:5173/?api=/api\n27: ```\n28: \n29: `/api` is same-origin (vite proxies it to `127.0.0.1:8080`, forwarding the\n30: bearer token). Served by the daemon itself (production, same origin) there\n31: is nothing to configure; against a remote daemon behind a reverse proxy the\n32: proxy serves both the UI and `/api`. For a non-loopback daemon bind, set the\n33: bearer token in the settings modal (`mg serve-token` writes one to the\n34: daemon's `.env` — tokens never ride in URLs).\n35: \n36: Development conveniences:\n37: \n38: - `?api=<url>` — point the session at a daemon without touching settings\n39:   (deep-link/testing only; tokens stay in the settings modal).\n40: - `?mock=1` (or `--mode mock`) — swap the API layer for the in-browser\n41:   fixture backend (`src/lib/api/mock.ts`), so the UI is fully explorable with\n42:   no daemon running. The mock mirrors the real API shapes exactly — its\n43:   routes are pinned by `mock.test.ts` so the dev environment cannot silently\n44:   drift from the shipped daemon.\n45: \n46: ## Layout\n47: \n48: ```\n49: src/\n50:   App.svelte            shell: rail, router, connection bar, palette\n51:   main.ts               bootstrap\n52:   lib/\n53:     api/                client, endpoint paths, types, mock backend, SSE stream\n54:     components/         Pipeline, MarkdownView, DiffView, RunConsole, modals, …\n55:     state/              connection, data (polling), toasts stores\n56:     views/              JobsView, JobDetailView, AgentsView, HealthView\n57:     diff.ts             parse git log/stat/patch into renderable structures\n58:     runlog.ts           parse run.log event timeline (incl. NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT)\n59:     markdown.ts         sanitized markdown render + verdict/status extraction\n60:     stage.ts            pipeline stage ordering + attention sorting\n61:     router.ts           hash router (#/p/<project>[/j/<job>[/<tab>]])\n62:     time.ts             relative time formatting\n63: ```\n64: \n65: ## Design notes\n66: \n67: - **Part 1 / Part 2 capability probing** — the client treats a 404/405 from a\n68:   mutating endpoint as a *capability miss* (`ApiError.capabilityMiss`), so\n69:   the same frontend runs against a read-only daemon (actions greyed out with\n70:   an explanation) and against the full control plane once job two's endpoints\n71:   land.\n72: - **Attention-first job list** — `stopped:needs-human` outranks `running`\n73:   outranks quiet; the segmented filter and the sort share one `stage.ts`.\n74: - **Live run console** — the Run tab polls `/jdi` for the event timeline and\n75:   attaches the `session.log` stream over SSE when the daemon offers it,\n76:   degrading to polling otherwise; the mode is shown, never hidden.\n77: - **Job files** — the daemon serves job files by their on-disk name\n78:   (`brief.md`, not `brief`); the client maps tab ids to filenames.\n79: - **Accessibility** — WCAG AA contrast on all informative text, keyboard\n80:   navigation throughout, ARIA roles on interactive affordances, verified per\n81:   render with the `shot` tool at 375/768/1280.\n\n(End of file - total 81 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# manigot web UI\n\nThe control-plane client for `mg serve` — a Svelte 5 single-page app that\nrenders the daemon's read-only API today and the mutating surface as it lands.\nIt is a port of the TUI's information design: same data, same job pipeline,\nsame attention ordering — built for a browser, so the \"review from a phone,\nget a ping when a job needs you, act on it\" story has a surface.\n\n## Running\n\n```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run dev        # vite dev server on :5173\nnpm run dev:mock   # same, with the in-browser mock daemon (no mg serve needed)\nnpm run build      # production build to dist/\nnpm run test       # vitest suite\n```\n\nThe app talks to the daemon through the connection setting (Settings modal /\n`?api=` URL param). The daemon is a same-origin JSON API — it sends no CORS","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/web-ui/README.md","text":"# manigot web UI\n\nThe control-plane client for `mg serve` — a Svelte 5 single-page app that\nrenders the daemon's read-only API today and the mutating surface as it lands.\nIt is a port of the TUI's information design: same data, same job pipeline,\nsame attention ordering — built for a browser, so the \"review from a phone,\nget a ping when a job needs you, act on it\" story has a surface.\n\n## Running\n\n```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run dev        # vite dev server on :5173\nnpm run dev:mock   # same, with the in-browser mock daemon (no mg serve needed)\nnpm run build      # production build to dist/\nnpm run test       # vitest suite\n```\n\nThe app talks to the daemon through the connection setting (Settings modal /\n`?api=` URL param). The daemon is a same-origin JSON API — it sends no CORS\nheaders, so the browser blocks any direct cross-origin URL (the error will\nsay \"cross-origin URL blocked\"). In dev, use the vite proxy path instead:\n\n```sh\nnpm run dev\n# open http://localhost:5173/?api=/api\n```\n\n`/api` is same-origin (vite proxies it to `127.0.0.1:8080`, forwarding the\nbearer token). Served by the daemon itself (production, same origin) there\nis nothing to configure; against a remote daemon behind a reverse proxy the\nproxy serves both the UI and `/api`. For a non-loopback daemon bind, set the\nbearer token in the settings modal (`mg serve-token` writes one to the\ndaemon's `.env` — tokens never ride in URLs).\n\nDevelopment conveniences:\n\n- `?api=<url>` — point the session at a daemon without touching settings\n  (deep-link/testing only; tokens stay in the settings modal).\n- `?mock=1` (or `--mode mock`) — swap the API layer for the in-browser\n  fixture backend (`src/lib/api/mock.ts`), so the UI is fully explorable with\n  no daemon running. The mock mirrors the real API shapes exactly — its\n  routes are pinned by `mock.test.ts` so the dev environment cannot silently\n  drift from the shipped daemon.\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nsrc/\n  App.svelte            shell: rail, router, connection bar, palette\n  main.ts               bootstrap\n  lib/\n    api/                client, endpoint paths, types, mock backend, SSE stream\n    components/         Pipeline, MarkdownView, DiffView, RunConsole, modals, …\n    state/              connection, data (polling), toasts stores\n    views/              JobsView, JobDetailView, AgentsView, HealthView\n    diff.ts             parse git log/stat/patch into renderable structures\n    runlog.ts           parse run.log event timeline (incl. NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT)\n    markdown.ts         sanitized markdown render + verdict/status extraction\n    stage.ts            pipeline stage ordering + attention sorting\n    router.ts           hash router (#/p/<project>[/j/<job>[/<tab>]])\n    time.ts             relative time formatting\n```\n\n## Design notes\n\n- **Part 1 / Part 2 capability probing** — the client treats a 404/405 from a\n  mutating endpoint as a *capability miss* (`ApiError.capabilityMiss`), so\n  the same frontend runs against a read-only daemon (actions greyed out with\n  an explanation) and against the full control plane once job two's endpoints\n  land.\n- **Attention-first job list** — `stopped:needs-human` outranks `running`\n  outranks quiet; the segmented filter and the sort share one `stage.ts`.\n- **Live run console** — the Run tab polls `/jdi` for the event timeline and\n  attaches the `session.log` stream over SSE when the daemon offers it,\n  degrading to polling otherwise; the mode is shown, never hidden.\n- **Job files** — the daemon serves job files by their on-disk name\n  (`brief.md`, not `brief`); the client maps tab ids to filenames.\n- **Accessibility** — WCAG AA contrast on all informative text, keyboard\n  navigation throughout, ARIA roles on interactive affordances, verified per\n  render with the `shot` tool at 375/768/1280.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":81,"totalLines":81,"truncated":false}},"title":"web-ui/README.md","time":{"start":1787992643365,"end":1787992643370}},"id":"prt_04caa97220016DtSpz4DwXVbpE","sessionID":"ses_fb3594f94ffeQ3bCtRbhDqaOUL","messageID":"msg_04caa7d1f0010woK2TrsKPzkIA"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787992643975,"sessionID":"ses_fb3594f94ffeQ3bCtRbhDqaOUL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_fd8929400a4e4beeaa9d7cb0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat /workspace/web-ui/package.json && ls /workspace/web-ui/src/lib/state /workspace/web-ui/src/lib/components/*.test.ts 2>/dev/null"},"output":"{\n  \"name\": \"manigot-web-ui\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"description\": \"manigot control plane — web client for the mg serve daemon\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"dev:mock\": \"vite --mode mock\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"preview\": \"vite preview\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n    \"test:watch\": \"vitest\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@fontsource-variable/familjen-grotesk\": \"^5.2.5\",\n    \"@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono\": \"^5.2.5\",\n    \"dompurify\": \"^3.2.6\",\n    \"marked\": \"^15.0.7\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte\": \"^5.0.3\",\n    \"@testing-library/jest-dom\": \"^6.6.3\",\n    \"@testing-library/svelte\": \"^5.2.1\",\n    \"jsdom\": \"^26.0.0\",\n    \"svelte\": \"^5.20.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.7.3\",\n    \"vite\": \"^6.1.0\",\n    \"vitest\": \"^3.0.6\"\n  }\n}\n/workspace/web-ui/src/lib/components/Pipeline.test.ts\n\n/workspace/web-ui/src/lib/state:\nconnection.svelte.ts\ndata.svelte.ts\ntoasts.svelte.ts\n","metadata":{"output":"{\n  \"name\": \"manigot-web-ui\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"description\": \"manigot control plane — web client for the mg serve daemon\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"dev:mock\": \"vite --mode mock\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"preview\": \"vite preview\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n    \"test:watch\": \"vitest\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@fontsource-variable/familjen-grotesk\": \"^5.2.5\",\n    \"@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono\": \"^5.2.5\",\n    \"dompurify\": \"^3.2.6\",\n    \"marked\": \"^15.0.7\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte\": \"^5.0.3\",\n    \"@testing-library/jest-dom\": \"^6.6.3\",\n    \"@testing-library/svelte\": \"^5.2.1\",\n    \"jsdom\": \"^26.0.0\",\n    \"svelte\": \"^5.20.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.7.3\",\n    \"vite\": \"^6.1.0\",\n    \"vitest\": \"^3.0.6\"\n  }\n}\n/workspace/web-ui/src/lib/components/Pipeline.test.ts\n\n/workspace/web-ui/src/lib/state:\nconnection.svelte.ts\ndata.svelte.ts\ntoasts.svelte.ts\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat /workspace/web-ui/package.json && ls /workspace/web-ui/src/lib/state /workspace/web-ui/src/lib/components/*.test.ts 2>/dev/null","time":{"start":1787992643965,"end":1787992643973}},"id":"prt_04caa9966001lbVgllLBs77iBi","sessionID":"ses_fb3594f94ffeQ3bCtRbhDqaOUL","messageID":"msg_04caa7d1f0010woK2TrsKPzkIA"}}
