{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1787995808541,"sessionID":"ses_fb3369276ffeikF3KayngIgfbM","part":{"id":"prt_04cdae31a001ga2RBoOmGcuU30","messageID":"msg_04cdade22001i6SRqF8JczR3N5","sessionID":"ses_fb3369276ffeikF3KayngIgfbM","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1787995812107,"sessionID":"ses_fb3369276ffeikF3KayngIgfbM","part":{"id":"prt_04cdae4de001hhU3SoEJ5bjr18","messageID":"msg_04cdade22001i6SRqF8JczR3N5","sessionID":"ses_fb3369276ffeikF3KayngIgfbM","type":"text","text":"Done. The job's connection-flow bugs are fixed and verified end-to-end against a real `mg serve` daemon.\n\n**Root cause found:** `web-ui/src/lib/router.ts`'s `navigate()` double-prefixed the hash. `href()` returns `#/p/manigot` but navigate wrapped it as `#${to}` → `##/p/manigot`, which `parseHash` cannot parse. So the home→jobs redirect never landed, and the landing stayed on \"Connecting to the daemon…\" even while the health check and project list were succeeding. On reload the stored hash was already single-`#`, which is exactly the reported \"works only after reload\" symptom — and the \"several pages stuck on Connecting\" symptom.\n\n**Fix** (`router.ts:50`): `navigate()` now strips a leading `#` before setting `location.hash`, so `navigate(href(...))` round-trips. This is on top of the branch's existing connection-store work (`established` edge triggering project loads, landing truth-telling for down/error/no-projects, `projectsError` surfacing, precise non-JSON errors) — all verified correct.\n\n**Tests:** added `navigate` single-hash round-trip tests (`router.test.ts`) and an App-level regression asserting the landing is left once a project is active (`App.test.ts`). Full suite: 87 passing; `vite build` succeeds.\n\n**Verified live** (real daemon on :8080 + vite `/api` proxy): fresh boot shows \"unreachable\" not \"Connecting\"; persisted connection and a settings save both populate the dropdown and redirect to the jobs page without reload; the health page renders the real `/health` response.\n\n`implementation.md` updated. (Session is read-only on git metadata — the host sweep-commit will pick up the changes.)","time":{"start":1787995808990,"end":1787995812104}}}
