{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787995938298,"sessionID":"ses_fb3250779ffe153rxsL511kCsf","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_22d203e54aec440e8bd83ffc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/balance_web-ui-connecting-to-the-daemon/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/balance_web-ui-connecting-to-the-daemon/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: web-ui: connecting to the daemon..\n2: \n3: id: balance\n4: status: open\n5: analyst:\n6: date:\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n9: \n10: ## Task breakdown\n11: \n12: <!-- TASK-1: description\n13:      files: list of files likely affected\n14:      depends: none\n15:      risk: low / medium / high — reason\n16: \n17: TASK-2: ...\n18: -->\n\n(End of file - total 18 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: web-ui: connecting to the daemon..\n\nid: balance\nstatus: open\nanalyst:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n<!-- TASK-1: description\n     files: list of files likely affected\n     depends: none\n     risk: low / medium / high — reason\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/balance_web-ui-connecting-to-the-daemon/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: web-ui: connecting to the daemon..\n\nid: balance\nstatus: open\nanalyst:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n<!-- TASK-1: description\n     files: list of files likely affected\n     depends: none\n     risk: low / medium / high — reason\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":18,"totalLines":18,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/balance_web-ui-connecting-to-the-daemon/tasks.md","time":{"start":1787995938292,"end":1787995938297}},"id":"prt_04cdcdcc1001x8lXYdlWfQmezt","sessionID":"ses_fb3250779ffe153rxsL511kCsf","messageID":"msg_04cdcd7a7001iv8NgQdgWCraZP"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787995938478,"sessionID":"ses_fb3250779ffe153rxsL511kCsf","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_930633185abf45668ae89064","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/balance_web-ui-connecting-to-the-daemon/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/balance_web-ui-connecting-to-the-daemon/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: web-ui: connecting to the daemon..\n2: \n3: id: balance\n4: status: open\n5: developer:\n6: date: 2026-08-29\n7: \n8: ## Summary\n9: \n10: Fixed the three connection-flow bugs in the web UI:\n11: \n12: 1. **Dropdown not populating after connection setup** — the project list now\n13:    loads off an `established` edge in the connection store (bumped on every\n14:    transition into `up`), reloaded once per establishment by an App-level\n15:    effect. A settings change, a first boot, or the daemon coming back all\n16:    repopulate the dropdown without a page reload.\n17: 2. **Pages stuck on \"Connecting to the daemon…\" despite a valid API** — root\n18:    cause was `router.navigate()` double-prefixing the fragment:\n19:    `href()` already returns `#/p/manigot`, and `navigate` wrapped it as\n20:    `#${to}` → `##/p/manigot`, which `parseHash` cannot parse, so the\n21:    home→jobs redirect never landed and the landing kept rendering. Fixed\n22:    `navigate` to strip the leading `#` first. The landing also now tells the\n23:    truth about the connection state instead of showing the message while\n24:    connected.\n25: 3. **Errors not reaching the user** — `/projects` failures set\n26:    `projectsError` (shown under the dropdown and on the landing); a 2xx that\n27:    is not JSON (mis-pointed connection, HTML fallback) is named precisely\n28:    instead of a JSON parse error.\n29: \n30: ## Changes\n31: \n32: - `web-ui/src/lib/router.ts` — `navigate()` now strips a leading `#` before\n33:   setting `location.hash` (single-fragment); `href()` falls home when no\n34:   project is active yet.\n35: - `web-ui/src/App.svelte` — bootstrap splits into `connection.check()` +\n36:   effect-driven `loadProjects()` keyed off `established`; landing branches on\n37:   down / projects error / no projects / connecting; dropdown surfaces the\n38:   projects error.\n39: - `web-ui/src/lib/state/connection.svelte.ts` — `established` counter,\n40:   `#gen` supersession so a re-pointed connection is never answered by a stale\n41:   in-flight response, `#inFlight` dedup across concurrent callers, and no\n42:   \"connecting\" flash on 30s re-validations.\n43: - `web-ui/src/lib/state/data.svelte.ts` — `projectsError` state; load failures\n44:   reach the UI instead of a silent empty dropdown.\n45: - `web-ui/src/lib/api/client.ts` — non-JSON 2xx bodies detected and named\n46:   (HTML vs other); precise CORS/unreachable error text on fetch failure.\n47: - `web-ui/src/lib/components/SettingsModal.svelte` — busy handling so the\n48:   modal always closes/keeps open on the right result.\n49: - Tests: `router.test.ts` (`navigate` single-hash round-trip, the regression),\n50:   `App.test.ts` (dropdown populates after settings change without reload,\n51:   redirect off the landing, empty-registry no-reload-loop, projects error\n52:   surfaced, health panel renders), `connection.test.ts`, `data.test.ts`,\n53:   `client.test.ts`.\n54: \n55: Verified end to end against a live `mg serve` (real daemon, vite `/api`\n56: proxy): fresh boot shows \"unreachable\" not \"Connecting to the daemon\";\n57: persisted connection populates the dropdown and redirects to the jobs page\n58: without a reload; settings save does the same; the health page renders the\n59: real `/health` response. Full vitest suite: 87 tests passing.\n60: \n61: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n62: \n63: - None in scope. (Pre-existing, unrelated a11y warnings from the Svelte\n64:   compiler in Modal/JobDetailView/RunConsole remain.)\n\n(End of file - total 64 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: web-ui: connecting to the daemon..\n\nid: balance\nstatus: open\ndeveloper:\ndate: 2026-08-29\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed the three connection-flow bugs in the web UI:\n\n1. **Dropdown not populating after connection setup** — the project list now\n   loads off an `established` edge in the connection store (bumped on every\n   transition into `up`), reloaded once per establishment by an App-level\n   effect. A settings change, a first boot, or the daemon coming back all\n   repopulate the dropdown without a page reload.\n2. **Pages stuck on \"Connecting to the daemon…\" despite a valid API** — root\n   cause was `router.navigate()` double-prefixing the fragment:\n   `href()` already returns `#/p/manigot`, and `navigate` wrapped it as\n   `#${to}` → `##/p/manigot`, which `parseHash` cannot parse, so the","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/balance_web-ui-connecting-to-the-daemon/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: web-ui: connecting to the daemon..\n\nid: balance\nstatus: open\ndeveloper:\ndate: 2026-08-29\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed the three connection-flow bugs in the web UI:\n\n1. **Dropdown not populating after connection setup** — the project list now\n   loads off an `established` edge in the connection store (bumped on every\n   transition into `up`), reloaded once per establishment by an App-level\n   effect. A settings change, a first boot, or the daemon coming back all\n   repopulate the dropdown without a page reload.\n2. **Pages stuck on \"Connecting to the daemon…\" despite a valid API** — root\n   cause was `router.navigate()` double-prefixing the fragment:\n   `href()` already returns `#/p/manigot`, and `navigate` wrapped it as\n   `#${to}` → `##/p/manigot`, which `parseHash` cannot parse, so the\n   home→jobs redirect never landed and the landing kept rendering. Fixed\n   `navigate` to strip the leading `#` first. The landing also now tells the\n   truth about the connection state instead of showing the message while\n   connected.\n3. **Errors not reaching the user** — `/projects` failures set\n   `projectsError` (shown under the dropdown and on the landing); a 2xx that\n   is not JSON (mis-pointed connection, HTML fallback) is named precisely\n   instead of a JSON parse error.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `web-ui/src/lib/router.ts` — `navigate()` now strips a leading `#` before\n  setting `location.hash` (single-fragment); `href()` falls home when no\n  project is active yet.\n- `web-ui/src/App.svelte` — bootstrap splits into `connection.check()` +\n  effect-driven `loadProjects()` keyed off `established`; landing branches on\n  down / projects error / no projects / connecting; dropdown surfaces the\n  projects error.\n- `web-ui/src/lib/state/connection.svelte.ts` — `established` counter,\n  `#gen` supersession so a re-pointed connection is never answered by a stale\n  in-flight response, `#inFlight` dedup across concurrent callers, and no\n  \"connecting\" flash on 30s re-validations.\n- `web-ui/src/lib/state/data.svelte.ts` — `projectsError` state; load failures\n  reach the UI instead of a silent empty dropdown.\n- `web-ui/src/lib/api/client.ts` — non-JSON 2xx bodies detected and named\n  (HTML vs other); precise CORS/unreachable error text on fetch failure.\n- `web-ui/src/lib/components/SettingsModal.svelte` — busy handling so the\n  modal always closes/keeps open on the right result.\n- Tests: `router.test.ts` (`navigate` single-hash round-trip, the regression),\n  `App.test.ts` (dropdown populates after settings change without reload,\n  redirect off the landing, empty-registry no-reload-loop, projects error\n  surfaced, health panel renders), `connection.test.ts`, `data.test.ts`,\n  `client.test.ts`.\n\nVerified end to end against a live `mg serve` (real daemon, vite `/api`\nproxy): fresh boot shows \"unreachable\" not \"Connecting to the daemon\";\npersisted connection populates the dropdown and redirects to the jobs page\nwithout a reload; settings save does the same; the health page renders the\nreal `/health` response. Full vitest suite: 87 tests passing.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- None in scope. (Pre-existing, unrelated a11y warnings from the Svelte\n  compiler in Modal/JobDetailView/RunConsole remain.)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":64,"totalLines":64,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/balance_web-ui-connecting-to-the-daemon/implementation.md","time":{"start":1787995938463,"end":1787995938476}},"id":"prt_04cdcde1b001zEbOHytn6ZAKp1","sessionID":"ses_fb3250779ffe153rxsL511kCsf","messageID":"msg_04cdcd7a7001iv8NgQdgWCraZP"}}
