{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787996355026,"sessionID":"ses_fb3250779ffe153rxsL511kCsf","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_4e28f890fcfe437c83886303","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"/workspace/bin/mg --help 2>&1 | head -20; echo \"=====\"; /workspace/bin/mg serve --help 2>&1 | head -30"},"output":"mg — isolated agent environment per project (Claude Code or OpenCode, sandboxed in Docker)\n\nProfiles bundle an agent CLI with one of your subscriptions. The built-ins are:\n  claude-pro        Claude Code, billed to your Claude Pro/Max subscription\n  zai               OpenCode, billed to your Z.AI Coding Plan\n  opencode-go       OpenCode, billed to the OpenCode Go subscription\n  opencode-zen      OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash)\n  opencode-zen-free OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash Free)\nYou can also define your own profiles (e.g. OpenCode Zen with a different\nmodel) with 'mg profiles add', stored in config/profiles.json.\n\nUsage:\n  mg                              Start a session in the current project\n  mg --profile <name>             ...with the given profile (claude-pro|zai|opencode-go|opencode-zen|opencode-zen-free)\n  mg --agent/-a <name>            Start straight in an agent (e.g. analyst)\n  mg --job/-j <id>                Start with a job's brief.md as the prompt\n  mg --agent <name> --job <id>    Combine the two\n\nCommands:\n  mg profiles [name|add|rm]      List the profiles (and which is the default),\n=====\nmg serve d3b0240-dirty\n\nThe listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API\nover a registry of project roots (the basis for the web UI / native GUI\ncontrol-plane sequence).\n\nUsage:\n  mg serve [flags]\n\nThe registry config file holds the named project roots the daemon serves:\n  {\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/project/root\"}, ...]}\n\"name\" is the URL segment the project is served under (a single URL-safe\npath segment, unique across the registry); it is required and chosen by you.\nDefault location: <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json (override with --registry).\nChanging the registered roots means editing the file and restarting.\n\nFlags:\n  -addr string\n    \tbind host (loopback default; a non-loopback bind requires a token) (default \"127.0.0.1\")\n  -port int\n    \tbind port (default 8080)\n  -registry string\n    \tpath to the project registry config (default <checkout>/config/serve.json)\n  -token string\n    \tbearer token required on every request (default $MG_SERVE_TOKEN)\n","metadata":{"output":"mg — isolated agent environment per project (Claude Code or OpenCode, sandboxed in Docker)\n\nProfiles bundle an agent CLI with one of your subscriptions. The built-ins are:\n  claude-pro        Claude Code, billed to your Claude Pro/Max subscription\n  zai               OpenCode, billed to your Z.AI Coding Plan\n  opencode-go       OpenCode, billed to the OpenCode Go subscription\n  opencode-zen      OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash)\n  opencode-zen-free OpenCode, billed to OpenCode Zen (DeepSeek V4 Flash Free)\nYou can also define your own profiles (e.g. OpenCode Zen with a different\nmodel) with 'mg profiles add', stored in config/profiles.json.\n\nUsage:\n  mg                              Start a session in the current project\n  mg --profile <name>             ...with the given profile (claude-pro|zai|opencode-go|opencode-zen|opencode-zen-free)\n  mg --agent/-a <name>            Start straight in an agent (e.g. analyst)\n  mg --job/-j <id>                Start with a job's brief.md as the prompt\n  mg --agent <name> --job <id>    Combine the two\n\nCommands:\n  mg profiles [name|add|rm]      List the profiles (and which is the default),\n=====\nmg serve d3b0240-dirty\n\nThe listener: a long-running daemon exposing a control API\nover a registry of project roots (the basis for the web UI / native GUI\ncontrol-plane sequence).\n\nUsage:\n  mg serve [flags]\n\nThe registry config file holds the named project roots the daemon serves:\n  {\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/project/root\"}, ...]}\n\"name\" is the URL segment the project is served under (a single URL-safe\npath segment, unique across the registry); it is required and chosen by you.\nDefault location: <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json (override with --registry).\nChanging the registered roots means editing the file and restarting.\n\nFlags:\n  -addr string\n    \tbind host (loopback default; a non-loopback bind requires a token) (default \"127.0.0.1\")\n  -port int\n    \tbind port (default 8080)\n  -registry string\n    \tpath to the project registry config (default <checkout>/config/serve.json)\n  -token string\n    \tbearer token required on every request (default $MG_SERVE_TOKEN)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"/workspace/bin/mg --help 2>&1 | head -20; echo \"=====\"; /workspace/bin/mg serve --help 2>&1 | head -30","time":{"start":1787996355022,"end":1787996355024}},"id":"prt_04ce338ec001xlyWICko10UkmP","sessionID":"ses_fb3250779ffe153rxsL511kCsf","messageID":"msg_04ce32ca4001wuqR06AnhytpX1"}}
